# WHAT VERCEL NEVER UPLOADS from web/ (the project's root directory).
#
# The test pages take ?rpc= and talk to a wallet, and on the production origin a
# crafted link to one would run with that origin's storage and wallet. They sit
# in web/ only because the browser tests serve web/ whole. web/_redirects answers
# the same paths with a 404 on Netlify, which has no ignore file.
#
# ONE LITERAL PATH PER LINE, from web/, with a leading slash - no wildcards:
# script/b20/check-publish-set.sh evaluates this file and refuses a line it
# cannot read exactly as Vercel does.
/tests.html
/wallet-setup.html
/wallet-stub.js
/REAL_WALLET_TEST.txt
/README.txt
/assets/README.txt
/vendor/README.txt
/e2e
/test-results
